%N A084863 Number of solutions to n = 2*u^2 + 3*v^2, u*v>0.
%C A084863 a(A084864(n)) > 0.
%H A084863 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/DiophantineEquation2ndPowers.html">Diophantine Equation: 2nd Powers.</a>
%F A084863 G.f.: (theta_3(q^2) - 1)*(theta_3(q^3) - 1)/4, where theta_3() is the Jacobi theta function. - _Ilya Gutkovskiy_, Sep 04 2026
%e A084863 n=770 = 2*19^2 + 3*4^2 = 2*17^2 + 3*8^2 = 2*13^2 + 3*12^2 = 2*1 +
%e A084863 3*16^2, therefore a(770)=4.
